## Rust ABAP LSP Project Rule

The repository root is a Rust workspace for the ABAP language server.

### Workspace layout

- `crates/abap_adt_cli` -> blocking CLI for SAP ADT repository search, source fetches, DDIC lookups, and child-object discovery.
- `crates/abap_jsonrpc` -> blocking JSON-RPC framing only.
- `crates/abap_lexer` -> tokenization, text ranges, low-level source utilities.
- `crates/abap_ast` -> syntax tree definitions and node helpers.
- `crates/abap_parser` -> syntax-only parser built on lexer + AST.
- `crates/abap_symbols` -> symbols, name resolution, semantic validation.
- `crates/abap_cache` -> workspace/document state, immutable snapshots, analysis publication.
- `crates/abap_lsp` -> LSP handlers, protocol-facing types, custom notifications.
- `crates/abap_lsp_server` -> executable entry point and blocking server loop.
- `editors/vscode` -> VS Code client and ADT-mediated remote dependency fetches.

### Dependency direction

Lower layers must not depend on higher layers:

- `abap_jsonrpc` is transport-only.
- `abap_lexer` has no ABAP higher-layer dependencies.
- `abap_ast` depends on `abap_lexer` only.
- `abap_parser` depends on `abap_lexer` and `abap_ast`.
- `abap_symbols` depends on `abap_lexer` and `abap_ast`.
- `abap_cache` depends on `abap_parser`, `abap_symbols`, and shared lower-level crates.
- `abap_lsp` depends on `abap_jsonrpc`, `abap_cache`, and protocol-related crates.
- `abap_lsp_server` depends on `abap_lsp` and `abap_jsonrpc`.

### Design defaults

- Avoid async unless there is a measured reason to introduce it.
- Prefer immutable published snapshots using `Arc`.
- Keep one foreground protocol loop and move CPU-heavy work into bounded worker pools.
- Keep SAP communication client-mediated first; the server should preserve the custom notification contract before attempting direct SAP transport.

### Commands

- Build: `.\build.bat`
- Release build: `.\build.bat release`
- Test: `.\test.bat`
- ADT CLI help: `cargo run -p abap_adt_cli -- --help`
- Build a package: `cargo build -p abap_lsp_server`
- Test a package: `cargo test -p abap_parser`

### Migration guidance

- Port tests with the crates they exercise rather than re-creating one monolithic root test suite.
- Profile before introducing specialized allocation strategies.


### Development standards

- Always ask before adding any new dependency or modifying versions of the existing dependencies.

### Remote SAP lookup

- When you need live SAP repository or DDIC data, prefer `abap-adt` over guessing or relying only on local files.
- Use it to look up ABAP source, classes, interfaces, reports, includes, function groups, function modules, tables, views, structures, table types, and data elements.
- Primary documentation: `docs/abap-adt-cli.md`
